//? Title: Styling a mepml document
//? Subtitle: one document, three looks
//? Style: paper.mepss

\abstract(
What a mepml document *is* and how it *looks* are two files. This one names a
style sheet in its header; change that line to `contrast.mepss`, or delete it
for mep's default look, and nothing else here changes.
)

> Text

Some *bold*, ~italic~, _underlined_, `verbatim`, |mono|, =highlighted=,
-struck-, +inserted+ and !deleted! text; a [link|https://example.org], a
>big< word and a <small> one; and maths, $e^{i\pi} + 1 = 0$.

>> Lists

- a bullet
  - a nested one
- [ ] an open task
- [x] a finished one
1. numbered

